  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cd96477d5695e8349a71dcd12e8bd8d2, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Hola again,


    Rosa here. My grandson says your shop is busier
    now. Bueno! Then you are ready for tamales.


    Tamales are never made alone.
    At Christmas my whole family sits around the table, spreading corn dough on husks,
    filling, folding, laughing, arguing. Three hundred tamales in one afternoon.


    Spread
    the dough thin, fill with pork and chili, fold tight, and steam them standing
    up.


    If you ever make tamales alone, invite someone next time. They taste
    better that way.'
